# Mock content vs translations

## Translations (`dictionaries/`)

UI chrome only: nav, page chrome, auth, player controls, shared labels.

Do **not** put demo catalog copy (teacher bios, routine descriptions, style/level taxonomy for sample data) in `dictionaries/`.

## Mocks (`mocks/`)

Demo/sample catalog until real production content exists:

- `mocks/content/{he,en}.json` — localized mock copy (styles, levels, chapters, routine text, teacher names/bios)
- `mocks/name-bank.ts` — seed pools for new demo rows
- `lib/routines.ts` / `lib/instructors.ts` — structural mock records (slugs, keys, media paths)

Rules:

- Do not treat bank names as final brand/legal choices
- Song/artist pairs are placeholder catalog examples (clearance/licensing TBD)
- Instagram URLs may be placeholders — replace only with URLs the user supplies
- Prefer pulling new demo rows from `mocks/name-bank.ts` instead of inventing one-off names
- Resolve mock copy with `getMockContent(locale)` / `lib/i18n/localize.ts`, not the UI dictionary
